What is the output?
class A { public: void show() { cout << "A"; } };
class B : public A { public: void show() { cout << "B"; } };
int main() { A *p = new B; p->show(); }

What is the output?
int n = 2;
switch (n) {
  case 1: printf("A");
  case 2: printf("B");
  case 3: printf("C"); break;
  default: printf("D");
}

What is the output of this program on a Unix system?
int main() {
  int x = 10;
  if (fork() == 0) { x = x + 5; printf("%d ", x); }
  else { wait(NULL); printf("%d ", x); }
  return 0;
}

What is the output of this C++ code?
